    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "804ec401_6f4fdf58",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-18T08:27:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure if that is possible. If it is then I think it would be quite complex and fragile. It would have to run after membership of the APEX was detected.\n\nAlso, I am not sure that behavior would actually be desirable as it would silently give any library within an APEX access to implementation details of a java_sdk_library within the same APEX. I think that decision should be up to the developers themselves. We already have some cases (sdk_version: \"\" or sdk_version: \"none\") where we silently expose users of java_sdk_library to the implementation details but at least the first is a known (and checked) source of incompatibility for APEX\u0027s and the latter is strictly limited in use.\n\nHaving an explicit reference to the .impl is good because it requires a developer\u0027s conscious decision makes it obvious to anyone reading it that something a bit special is going on.",
      "parentUuid": "aa974a79_28071814",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "50f090daaf4212dc54f538f4f2a646d6a9b896b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bdcea804_99e6bbd2",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-18T08:53:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s doable because that\u0027s how the linking is done for the native libs. And yes, it has to run after the membership of the APEX was detected. What is being done for the native side is that we add two dependencies - one for the stub, the other for the impl - during the deps mutator and choose one in GenerateAndroidBuildActions that is far after the membership is determined.\n\nDeveloper\u0027s conscious decision is a good thing, but I think it\u0027s more valuable to give consistent mental model to them. If the way things work differ across native and java world, that will increase the confusion.\n\nEven when *.impl can be explicitly specified, it should be allowed only within the same APEX, which means we need an additional check routine.",
      "parentUuid": "804ec401_6f4fdf58",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "50f090daaf4212dc54f538f4f2a646d6a9b896b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
